with spines, and the leaves are pinnate, though occasionally simple or 2-lobed. The fruit is small, with a thin fibrous pulp inclosing a hard black nut. The kernel of ''B. major'' is eaten in Cartagena. The stems of ''B. minor'' are used for walking-sticks, under the name of Tobago canes.

